{"kind":"promise","text":"I will build the GitHub connector's inbound half, starting with the charter, since nothing may append under it until hugh ratifies it.\n\nI will draft the charter as a durable statement naming the watched repository, the connector's actor key, the event mapping, and the doorstep, and file it for ratification rather than assuming an answer. The doorstep in particular is hugh's to set: whether any GitHub account filing an issue may cause a durable act in this log, or only some. I will state the options and my recommendation, and wait.\n\nWhile that is open I will build the parts that do not depend on the answer: the observe path itself, keyed idempotency through the intent namespace so redelivery collapses to a replay, the correspondence fold over durable acts rather than any private database, and the surface-ownership rule that keeps the connector from reading back its own writing. The connector will run as a separate command holding its own key and submitting through the existing public surface, with no change to the kernel or the fold."}